+/// EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD_ALL_READS=1 (with =2 or =3; off by default). Port of yuri2301/Eglantine
+/// c5145ace9 (yuri2301, "frame overlap copies", 11 Nov 2026): there the copies a guest write
+/// takes for the frame in flight serve EVERY read the GPU side makes of guest memory, not only
+/// the buffer cache's. Here the guard's copies also serve
+///  - DeviceMemoryManager::ReadBlock / ReadBlockUnsafe (texture uploads through GpuGuestMemory,
+///    the DMA engine, everything that reads device memory by block),
+///  - Tegra::MemoryManager::ReadBlock / ReadBlockUnsafe (descriptor tables, small descriptor
+///    reads, macro and inline data), and
+///  - DeviceMemoryManager::GetSpan, which returns no span for a range with a copy, so its caller
+///    reads it by block (as for a range that is not continuous).
+/// The copy's bytes go over what the read took from memory, after the read, so a write that
+/// copied its page while the read ran is still covered. What a read took from a copy is handed
+/// back as a guest write once its frame is passed or lifted (TakeRedirty), as for uploads, so a
+/// texture uploaded from a copy is uploaded again from memory. Implies
+/// EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD_ALL_WRITES=1 unless that is set (yuri's copies are taken for every page
+/// the caches hold, which is what ALL_WRITES does). Upstream measured, PC, village spawn point: 44 ->
+/// 31.5 ms a frame, a frame ahead with no one-frame flashes in 450 frames; all of its hits were
+/// buffer uploads, which our guard covered already. Line: "EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD_ALL_READS: last
+/// 300 presents ...". Unset: nothing changes (one bool test per block read).
+inline bool AllReads() {
